  "body": "Two Orthographic-view follow-ups found while fixing #600 (that depth fix is carried by #604). This branch is off main and doesn't depend on #604; its tests check the ray and camera math on the CPU.\n\n## #609: the traced stock casts parallel rays in ortho (`7b9800d1`)\n- **`PreviewCamera`** (sim `stock_sim/preview.rs`):\n  - a new `ortho_half_height: Option<f64>`;\n  - `orthographic(h)`, which refuses a non-finite or non-positive half height by name;\n  - `ray(px, py, w, h) -> (origin, dir)`. In ortho, each pixel's ray starts on the eye plane and runs along the view direction, matching `Camera::mvp` and `ray_through`. Perspective is unchanged.\n- **Who uses the same rule:** the CPU march, the GPU march (`trace.wgsl`, via the unused `world_lo.w`) and the compositor (`composite.wgsl`, via `frame.z`).\n- **Viewport wiring:** `eye_geom::preview_camera` takes the half height from the viewport camera, and the cache key includes it, so switching modes re-traces.\n\n## #610: vertex-pick visibility in ortho (`4d9922b1`)\n- `vertex_pick::sight_origin`: perspective starts at the eye as before. Ortho starts at the corner's own point on the eye plane, so the test runs back along the view direction, as `ray_through` does.\n- A corner at or behind the eye plane is not offered.\n\n## How tested\n- **sim `stock_preview::an_orthographic_eye_casts_parallel_rays_from_its_view_plane`:** parallel rays from the eye plane, the box top at one depth, misses off the footprint, perspective unchanged, and a bad half height refused.\n- **ui `trace::eye_geom::tests::the_traced_stock_lands_on_the_mesh_pixel_in_both_projections`:** all 8 corners of a stock box, projected through `Camera::mvp`, lie on their pixel's traced ray in both projections. With the fix reverted, a corner misses by 2.81 against a pixel width of 0.80.\n- **ui `vertex_pick_tests::orthographic_visibility_runs_along_the_view_direction_not_to_the_eye`:** an occluder on the parallel ray hides a corner, and an occluder only on the line to the eye doesn't. The old test got both backwards.\n- **Gate:** ui lib 378, stock_preview 11, gpu_render, trace_composite and trace_parity pass. Clippy is clean (ui, sim, app).\n- **Shaders:** both pass naga 30.0.1's parser and validator. **This machine has no wgpu adapter, so the GPU and compositor paths weren't exercised; a review on a machine with an adapter should run gpu_render, trace_composite and trace_parity.**\n\nChangelog: Orthographic view: the traced stock sim view now casts parallel rays, so it lines up with the ortho-drawn part, meshes and toolpaths (#609)\nChangelog: Orthographic view: vertex picking tests visibility along the parallel view direction, so a hidden corner is no longer offered and a visible one is no longer refused (#610)\n\nFixes #609\nFixes #610\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
